    if True, use the residue types of the database fragments, otherwise name the residues \"UNK\"
";

%feature("docstring") hole "
find the pore (channel) through a molecule between two points

Run Coot's HOLE-like channel/pore analysis: a probe is passed along the line from the start point to the end point and the maximum radius that fits at each step is found. The pore surface is displayed as a generic display object (\"Probe surface\"), a dialog with the probe radius as a function of distance along the path is shown, and the radius profile is also written to the file probe-radius.tab in the current directory. If a valid refinement map is set ( imol_refinement_map() ) the map around the pore is also written to hole.map .

  imol  the model molecule index   start_x  x coordinate of the start point (Å)   start_y  y coordinate of the start point (Å)   start_z  z coordinate of the start point (Å)   end_x  x coordinate of the end point (Å)   end_y  y coordinate of the end point (Å)   end_z  z coordinate of the end point (Å)   colour_map_multiplier  scale applied to the radius-to-colour mapping of the surface (the GUI uses 1.0)   colour_map_offset  offset applied to the radius-to-colour mapping of the surface (the GUI uses 0.0)   n_runs  currently unused   show_probe_radius_graph_flag  currently unused (the probe radius text dialog is always shown)   export_surface_dots_file_name  if not empty, write the surface dots to this file (one line per dot: x y z red green blue hex-colour)

Parameters
----------
imol : int
    the model molecule index
start_x : float
    x coordinate of the start point (Å)
start_y : float
    y coordinate of the start point (Å)
start_z : float
    z coordinate of the start point (Å)
end_x : float
    x coordinate of the end point (Å)
end_y : float
    y coordinate of the end point (Å)
end_z : float
    z coordinate of the end point (Å)
colour_map_multiplier : float
    scale applied to the radius-to-colour mapping of the surface (the GUI uses 1.0)
colour_map_offset : float
    offset applied to the radius-to-colour mapping of the surface (the GUI uses 0.0)
n_runs : int
    currently unused
show_probe_radius_graph_flag : bool
    currently unused (the probe radius text dialog is always shown)
export_surface_dots_file_name : str
    if not empty, write the surface dots to this file (one line per dot: x y z red green blue hex-colour)
";

