%feature("docstring") map_to_model_correlation "
Calculate the correlation between a map and model for specific residues.

This function calculates the correlation between the observed map and a map calculated from the selected atoms of the specified residues, over the grid points within the atom radius (see set_map_correlation_atom_radius() ), excluding grid points that overlap with neighboring residues.

  imol  Model molecule number   residue_specs  Vector of residue specifications to evaluate   neigh_residue_specs  Vector of neighboring residues whose grid points should be excluded   atom_mask_mode  Controls which atoms are included in the calculation:  0: All atoms 1: Main-chain atoms if standard amino acid, else all atoms 2: Side-chain atoms if standard amino acid, else all atoms 3: Side-chain atoms excluding CB if standard amino acid, else all atoms 4: Main-chain atoms if standard amino acid, else nothing 5: Side-chain atoms if standard amino acid, else nothing 10: All atoms, with the atom radius dependent on the atom's B-factor   imol_map  Map molecule number to correlate against Correlation coefficient (float) between model and map (nan on failure, e.g. invalid molecules or no grid points) In the current implementation, modes 4 and 5 select all atoms (rather than main-chain or side-chain atoms) for standard amino acids. Use this after refinement to evaluate if the fit improved Example: std::vector<coot::residue_spec_t> residues = {{chain_id, 40, \"\" }, {chain_id, 41, \"\" }}; std::vector<coot::residue_spec_t> neighbors; float corr = map_to_model_correlation (1, residues, neighbors, 2, 2);

Parameters
----------
imol : int
    Model molecule number
residue_specs : list
    Vector of residue specifications to evaluate
neigh_residue_specs : list
    Vector of neighboring residues whose grid points should be excluded
atom_mask_mode : unsigned short int
    Controls which atoms are included in the calculation:  0: All atoms 1: Main-chain atoms if standard amino acid, else all atoms 2: Side-chain atoms if standard amino acid, else all atoms 3: Side-chain atoms excluding CB if standard amino acid, else all atoms 4: Main-chain atoms if standard amino acid, else nothing 5: Side-chain atoms if standard amino acid, else nothing 10: All atoms, with the atom radius dependent on the atom's B-factor
imol_map : int
    Map molecule number to correlate against
";

%feature("docstring") map_to_model_correlation_stats "
Get the map-to-model correlation statistics for a set of residues.

A model map is calculated from the selected atoms of residue_specs and compared with the map imol_map over the grid points that lie within the map-correlation atom radius of those atoms (1.5 Å by default, see set_map_correlation_atom_radius() ). Grid points within that radius of the atoms of neigh_residue_specs are excluded, so that density belonging to neighbouring residues does not contribute.

  imol  the model molecule index   residue_specs  the residues to evaluate   neigh_residue_specs  neighbouring residues whose atoms mask out grid points   atom_mask_mode  which atoms of each residue are used:  0: all atoms 1: main-chain atoms if a standard amino acid, else all atoms 2: side-chain atoms if a standard amino acid, else all atoms 3: side-chain atoms excluding CB if a standard amino acid, else all atoms 4: main-chain atoms if a standard amino acid, else nothing 5: side-chain atoms if a standard amino acid, else nothing 10: all atoms with a B-factor-dependent radius   imol_map  the map molecule index a coot::util::density_correlation_stats_info_t: the accumulated sums ( n , sum_x , sum_y , sum_xy , sum_sqrd_x , sum_sqrd_y , where x is the model-calculated map and y is imol_map ) and the sampled map values ( density_values ). Use its correlation() , var_x() and var_y() member functions. If imol is not a valid model or imol_map is not a valid map (or no atoms were selected) the returned object is empty ( n is 0). Example: auto stats = map_to_model_correlation_stats (1, residues, neighbors, 0, 2); std::cout << \"Correlation: \" << stats.correlation() << \" from \" << stats.n << \" points\" << std::endl;

Parameters
----------
imol : int
    the model molecule index
residue_specs : list
    the residues to evaluate
neigh_residue_specs : list
    neighbouring residues whose atoms mask out grid points
atom_mask_mode : unsigned short int
    which atoms of each residue are used:  0: all atoms 1: main-chain atoms if a standard amino acid, else all atoms 2: side-chain atoms if a standard amino acid, else all atoms 3: side-chain atoms excluding CB if a standard amino acid, else all atoms 4: main-chain atoms if a standard amino acid, else nothing 5: side-chain atoms if a standard amino acid, else nothing 10: all atoms with a B-factor-dependent radius
imol_map : int
    the map molecule index
";

%feature("docstring") map_to_model_correlation_per_residue "
Get map-to-model correlation per residue.

Returns individual correlation values (model-calculated map vs imol_map ) for each residue, using grid points within 1.5 Å of the selected atoms. Grid points that are within that radius of atoms of more than one residue are excluded. Useful for identifying which specific residues fit poorly.

  imol  the model molecule index   specs  the residues to evaluate. Note: with atom_mask_mode 0 the atom selection is the whole molecule, so a correlation is returned for every residue in the molecule, not only for those in specs .   atom_mask_mode  which atoms to include (0: all atoms, 1: main-chain, 2: side-chain, 3: side-chain excluding CB - for non-standard residues these use all atoms; 4: main-chain, 5: side-chain - for non-standard residues these use no atoms)   imol_map  the map molecule index a vector of (residue_spec, correlation) pairs. Residues with fewer than 2 contributing grid points are omitted. Empty if imol or imol_map is not valid. Example: auto correlations = map_to_model_correlation_per_residue (1, specs, 0, 2); // Sort by correlation (lowest first) std::sort(correlations.begin(), correlations.end(), []( const auto &a, const auto &b) { return a.second < b.second; }); // First element is now the worst-fitting residue std::cout << \"Worst residue: \" << correlations[0].first << \" correlation: \" << correlations[0].second << std::endl;

Parameters
----------
imol : int
    the model molecule index
specs : list
    the residues to evaluate. Note: with atom_mask_mode 0 the atom selection is the whole molecule, so a correlation is returned for every residue in the molecule, not only for those in specs .
atom_mask_mode : unsigned short int
    which atoms to include (0: all atoms, 1: main-chain, 2: side-chain, 3: side-chain excluding CB - for non-standard residues these use all atoms; 4: main-chain, 5: side-chain - for non-standard residues these use no atoms)
imol_map : int
    the map molecule index
";

%feature("docstring") map_to_model_correlation_stats_per_residue "
Get map density statistics per residue.

Despite the name, this does not calculate a correlation: for each residue it accumulates the values of imol_map at the grid points within atom_radius_for_masking of the residue's selected atoms. Grid points that are within that radius of atoms of more than one residue are excluded.

  imol  the model molecule index   residue_specs  the residues to evaluate   atom_mask_mode  which atoms to include (as for map_to_model_correlation_stats() )   atom_radius_for_masking  the masking radius around each atom (in Å, typically 1.5)   imol_map  the map molecule index a map of residue_spec to coot::util::density_stats_info_t (members n , sum , sum_sq , sum_weight ; use mean_and_variance() to get the mean and variance of the density). Empty if imol or imol_map is not valid. Example: auto stats_map = map_to_model_correlation_stats_per_residue (1, specs, 0, 1.5, 2); for ( const auto &pair : stats_map) { std::pair<double, double> mv = pair.second.mean_and_variance(); std::cout << pair.first << \": mean=\" << mv.first << \" var=\" << mv.second << std::endl; }

Parameters
----------
imol : int
    the model molecule index
residue_specs : list
    the residues to evaluate
atom_mask_mode : unsigned short int
    which atoms to include (as for map_to_model_correlation_stats() )
atom_radius_for_masking : float
    the masking radius around each atom (in Å, typically 1.5)
imol_map : int
    the map molecule index
";

%feature("docstring") map_to_model_correlation_stats_per_residue_range "
Get map-to-model correlation statistics for runs of residues along a chain.

The chain is split into overlapping windows of n_residue_per_residue_range residues; the correlation of the model-calculated map with imol_map over each window is reported against the middle residue of that window. Windows that include waters, nucleotides or HETATM residues are skipped. The atom mask radius is 2.8 Å; a grid point within that radius of several atoms is counted once for each of them.

  imol  the model molecule index   chain_id  the chain id (e.g. \"A\")   imol_map  the map molecule index   n_residue_per_residue_range  the number of residues per window (e.g. 1, 3 or 5)   exclude_NOC_flag  if non-zero, split the statistics into main-chain and side-chain. The split is made by atom: the grid points around atoms that lie within 1.8 Å of a main-chain N, C, O or H atom (i.e. N, C, O, H, CA and the CD of proline) are main-chain, the grid points around the other atoms are side-chain. a pair of maps from (middle) residue spec to coot::util::density_correlation_stats_info_t:  first: all-atom statistics if exclude_NOC_flag is zero, main-chain statistics otherwise second: side-chain statistics (only filled with data when exclude_NOC_flag is set, otherwise the entries have n = 0 and the correlation is nan) Both maps are empty if imol or imol_map is not valid.

Example: auto [all_atom_stats, sidechain_stats] = map_to_model_correlation_stats_per_residue_range (1, \"A\" , 2, 1, 0); // Find worst-fitting residue (all atoms) auto worst = std::min_element( all_atom_stats.begin(), all_atom_stats.end(), []( const auto &a, const auto &b) { return a.second.correlation() < b.second.correlation(); } );

Parameters
----------
imol : int
    the model molecule index
chain_id : str
    the chain id (e.g. \"A\")
imol_map : int
    the map molecule index
n_residue_per_residue_range : int
    the number of residues per window (e.g. 1, 3 or 5)
exclude_NOC_flag : int
    if non-zero, split the statistics into main-chain and side-chain. The split is made by atom: the grid points around atoms that lie within 1.8 Å of a main-chain N, C, O or H atom (i.e. N, C, O, H, CA and the CD of proline) are main-chain, the grid points around the other atoms are side-chain.
";

