";

%feature("docstring") colour_map_by_other_map_py "
colour a map by another map, using a colour table

The colour_table should be a list of colours, each a list [r, g, b] (0 to 1). So, if the colour table has 4 entries covering the range from 0 to 1, then table_bin_start would be 0, the table_bin_size would be 0.25 and the colour_table list would have 4 entries covering the range 0->0.25, 0.25->0.5, 0.5->0.75, 0.75->1.0 Values in imol_map_used_for_colouring outside the table range take the colour at the ends of the range.

  imol_map  the map molecule index   imol_map_used_for_colouring  the index of the map whose values determine the colours   table_bin_start  the map value at the start of the colour table   table_bin_size  the range of map values covered by each colour table entry   colour_table_list  a list of [r, g, b] colours

Parameters
----------
imol_map : int
    the map molecule index
imol_map_used_for_colouring : int
    the index of the map whose values determine the colours
table_bin_start : float
    the map value at the start of the colour table
table_bin_size : float
    the range of map values covered by each colour table entry
colour_table_list : object
    a list of [r, g, b] colours
";

