%feature("docstring") check_waters_baddies "
find \"bad\" waters in a model molecule

Tests the HOH/WAT residues of molecule imol against the density of the refinement map (set with set_imol_refinement_map() ), their B-factors and their distances to other atoms. If the graphics interface is in use, the \"checked waters baddies\" dialog is also shown.

Note that this does not itself check that the refinement map is valid.

  imol  the model molecule index   b_factor_lim  waters with a B-factor above this are flagged. A negative value disables this test.   map_sigma_lim  waters with density (in units of the map rmsd) below this are flagged. Pass a large negative value (e.g. -100) to disable this test.   min_dist  waters closer than this (in Å) to their nearest (non-hydrogen) atom are flagged. A negative value disables this test.   max_dist  waters further than this (in Å) from their nearest (non-hydrogen) atom are flagged. A negative value disables this test.   part_occ_contact_flag  if non-zero, the distance tests are skipped   zero_occ_flag  if non-zero, waters with zero occupancy are excluded from the distance tests   logical_operator_and_or_flag  0 means combine the criteria with logical AND, otherwise logical OR (a water is flagged if it fails any test) a vector of the atom specs of the flagged water atoms (empty if imol is not a valid model molecule)

Parameters
----------
imol : int
    the model molecule index
b_factor_lim : float
    waters with a B-factor above this are flagged. A negative value disables this test.
map_sigma_lim : float
    waters with density (in units of the map rmsd) below this are flagged. Pass a large negative value (e.g. -100) to disable this test.
min_dist : float
    waters closer than this (in Å) to their nearest (non-hydrogen) atom are flagged. A negative value disables this test.
max_dist : float
    waters further than this (in Å) from their nearest (non-hydrogen) atom are flagged. A negative value disables this test.
part_occ_contact_flag : int
    if non-zero, the distance tests are skipped
zero_occ_flag : int
    if non-zero, waters with zero occupancy are excluded from the distance tests
logical_operator_and_or_flag : int
    0 means combine the criteria with logical AND, otherwise logical OR (a water is flagged if it fails any test)
";

%feature("docstring") find_blobs "
find blobs of unmodelled density

The map is masked by the atoms of the model (mask radius 1.9 Å; waters are masked or not according to set_find_ligand_mask_waters() ) and then clusters of grid points above the cut-off are found. Only clusters that are too big to be a water are returned.

  imol_model  the model molecule index   imol_map  the map molecule index   cut_off_density_level  the cut-off in units of the map rmsd (σ) a vector of (blob centre, blob volume in Å^3) pairs, in order of decreasing summed density. Empty on failure.

Parameters
----------
imol_model : int
    the model molecule index
imol_map : int
    the map molecule index
cut_off_density_level : float
    the cut-off in units of the map rmsd (σ)
";

%feature("docstring") find_blobs_scm "
find blobs of unmodelled density - scheme interface

See find_blobs()

  imol_model  the model molecule index   imol_map  the map molecule index   cut_off_density_level  the cut-off in units of the map rmsd (σ) a list of blobs, each of the form (volume x y z), or #f if either molecule index is invalid

Parameters
----------
imol_model : int
    the model molecule index
imol_map : int
    the map molecule index
cut_off_density_level : float
    the cut-off in units of the map rmsd (σ)
";

%feature("docstring") find_blobs_py "
Find regions of unmodelled density (\"blobs\") in a map.

Identifies regions of significant density that are not explained by the current atomic model - e.g. missing ligands, cofactors or residues.

The map is masked by the atoms of imol_model (mask radius 1.9 Å; whether or not waters are used for masking is controlled by set_find_ligand_mask_waters() ). Clusters of grid points above the cut-off are then found. Clusters that are small enough to be a water (volume < 11 Å^3) are not returned - only the \"big blobs\" are.

Only positive density is considered.

  imol_model  the model molecule index. Density explained by the atoms of this model is masked out.   imol_map  the map molecule index (typically a 2mFo-DFc or mFo-DFc map)   cut_off_sigma_density_level  the cut-off in units of the map rmsd (σ), e.g. 1.0 for a 2mFo-DFc map or 3.0 for a difference map a list of blobs, or False if imol_model is not a valid model molecule or imol_map is not a valid map molecule. Each blob is a 2-element list: [[x, y, z], volume], where the position is the blob centre (orthogonal coordinates in Å) and volume is the volume of the blob in Å^3. The blobs are ordered by decreasing summed density. blobs = coot.find_blobs_py(0, 1, 1.0) if blobs: for position, volume in blobs: print(position, volume) # go to the first (strongest) blob x, y, z = blobs[0][0] coot.set_rotation_centre(x, y, z)

Parameters
----------
imol_model : int
    the model molecule index. Density explained by the atoms of this model is masked out.
imol_map : int
    the map molecule index (typically a 2mFo-DFc or mFo-DFc map)
cut_off_sigma_density_level : float
    the cut-off in units of the map rmsd (σ), e.g. 1.0 for a 2mFo-DFc map or 3.0 for a difference map
";

